cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "UMAT-OTI: Deterministic order-truncated imaginary tangent generation for Abaqus UMATs"
abstract: >-
  UMAT-OTI transforms Abaqus user-material subroutine (UMAT) Fortran source so
  that the consistent material tangent (DDSDDE) is computed by order-truncated
  imaginary (OTI) automatic differentiation instead of hand-coded or
  finite-difference derivatives, driven by a compact JSON contract.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-21"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AMMS-Lab-UTSA/UMAT_source_transformation"
url: "https://github.com/AMMS-Lab-UTSA/UMAT_source_transformation"
keywords:
  - Abaqus
  - UMAT
  - automatic differentiation
  - order-truncated imaginary numbers
  - consistent tangent
  - finite element method
  - constitutive models
